# Browser only: a text field takes typing through the page's own <input> (what a phone's on-screen
# keyboard and an IME need), not through the canvas. Needs a typist, so it is not in the
# scripts/verify/*.cmds loops:
#   node scripts/web/run_in_browser.mjs scripts/verify/browser/text_field_page.cmds --type-into-field "Ada"
# The runner types "Ada" (trusted input, like an IME commit) once the page input has the focus.
# Expected picture:
#   text_field_page.png: the "Greeting" panel at the top right, the field holds "Ada" (lighter: it
#                        has the focus), "Hello, Ada!" at the bottom centre.

ui.show_panel greeting
wait 2
ui.focus_field greeting name
wait_until 3000 assert.ui_field greeting name Ada
assert.ui_focused greeting name
ui.press greeting greet
wait 2
assert.ui_text greeting_text Hello, Ada!
snapshot text_field_page
quit
